  "slug": "bilayer-graphene-energy-spectrum-3476",
  "summary": "Three November 2026 preprints revisit energy spectra in bilayer graphene and related few-body systems using deformed-algebra and quantum Monte Carlo methods.",
  "synthesis": "The common scientific thread is the computation of energy spectra in two-dimensional and few-body quantum systems. Two preprints address bilayer graphene directly. One derives spectra, currents, and thermodynamics for q-deformed Dirac oscillator models of monolayer and bilayer graphene in a magnetic field. The other applies momentum-space quantum Monte Carlo to twisted bilayer graphene, explicitly including remote bands and testing the validity of flat-band projection. The distinctive elements are the deformed-algebra treatment of the magnetic-field problem and the explicit assessment of interaction effects beyond projected flat-band models in the twisted case. A third preprint computes trion energy levels in bulk semiconductors across hole-to-electron mass ratios using finite-element and Gaussian expansion methods. It shares the spectral-calculation approach but not the graphene context.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-21"
}
